# 25. Troubleshooting NetworkPolicy

When network communication stops working, check:

### Check Pods

```bash
kubectl get pods -o wide
```

### Check Services

```bash
kubectl get svc
```

### Check NetworkPolicies

```bash
kubectl get networkpolicy
```

### Describe policy

```bash
kubectl describe networkpolicy <policy-name>
```

### Check Pod labels

```bash
kubectl get pods --show-labels
```

This is especially important because selectors depend on labels.

### Test connectivity

A temporary debugging Pod can be useful:

```bash
kubectl run test-pod \
  --image=curlimages/curl \
  --rm -it \
  -- sh
```

Then test connectivity from inside the cluster.

