# 26. Common NetworkPolicy Mistakes

### Mistake 1 — Wrong labels

Policy:

```yaml
podSelector:
  matchLabels:
    app: backend
```

But Pod:

```yaml
labels:
  app: api
```

Then the policy doesn't select that Pod.

---

### Mistake 2 — Forgetting Egress

You may allow:

```text
Frontend → Backend
```

but forget that backend also needs:

```text
Backend → Database
```

If egress isolation is enabled, that connection may be blocked unless explicitly allowed.

---

### Mistake 3 — Blocking DNS

A strict egress policy may accidentally prevent:

```text
Pod → CoreDNS
```

which can cause domain-name resolution failures.

---

### Mistake 4 — Assuming Service is selected

NetworkPolicy doesn't select:

```text
Service
```

It selects:

```text
Pods
```

using selectors.

---

### Mistake 5 — Assuming Kubernetes itself enforces every policy

The CNI must support and enforce NetworkPolicy.

